[Id "immortal"]
[Name "The Immortal Game"]
[White "Adolf Anderssen"]
[Black "Lionel Kieseritzky"]
[Event "London (a casual game)"]
[Date "1851"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Source "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immortal_Game"]
[Blurb "Played for fun during a break in the London 1851 tournament. Anderssen gives up a bishop, both rooks and his queen, then mates with his three remaining minor pieces. Kieseritzky is said to have resigned before the end, so the last moves may never have been played."]

1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Bc4 Qh4+ 4. Kf1 b5 5. Bxb5 Nf6 6. Nf3 Qh6 7. d3 Nh5 8.
