Nxg7+ Kd8 22. Qf6+ Nxf6 23. Be7# 1-0

[Id "evergreen"]
[Name "The Evergreen Game"]
[White "Adolf Anderssen"]
[Black "Jean Dufresne"]
[Event "Berlin (probably a casual game)"]
[Date "1852"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Source "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evergreen_Game"]
[Blurb "Steinitz named it after the quiet 19.Rad1, which sets a trap that Black walks straight into. The finish is a queen sacrifice on d7 and a mate by the two bishops, 24.Bxe7#."]

