[Id "opera"]
[Name "The Opera Game"]
[White "Paul Morphy"]
[Black "Duke Karl of Brunswick and Count Isouard"]
[Event "Paris, in a box at the opera"]
[Date "1858"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Source "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opera_Game"]
[Blurb "Morphy played it in a box at the Paris opera during a performance, against two noblemen choosing Black's moves together. He develops fast, sacrifices freely and mates on move 17. Teachers still use it to show why development matters."]

